    "title": "April 29 to be Recognized as National Fentanyl Awareness Day - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 days ago CARTERVILLE, Ill. (WSIL) -- The U.S. Drug Enforcement Administration will recognize National Fentanyl Awareness Day on April 29 as a show of support for partners in law enforcement, public health and non-profit agencies. Fentanyl-related deaths have decreased in recent years, yet fentanyl remains the leading cause of death among Americans ages 18 to 45. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 3",
